  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1064",
      "html": "<ul><li><strong>Scientific name:</strong> Rineloricaria eigenmanni (Pellegrin, 1908)</li><li><strong>Common name:</strong> Common Whiptail Catfish</li><li><strong>Type locality:</strong> Sarare, Venezuela</li><li><strong>Size:</strong> 102 mm (4 in) SL</li><li><strong>IUCN Red List:</strong> Least Concern (last assessed 2020)</li><li><strong>Etymology:</strong> Greek rhinos = nose + Latin lorica, loricare = cuirass or corslet of leather. Named in honour of Dr. Carl H. Eigenmann, Professor of Ichthyology in Indiana (1863-1927).</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1064",
      "html": "<p>South America: Orinoco drainage basin.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1064",
      "html": "<p>Habitat photo: Venezuelan llanos in the dry season.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1064",
      "html": "<ul><li>pH: 6.0 - 7.4</li><li>Temperature: 24.0-29.0°C (75.2-84.2°F)</li><li>Needs neutral, soft water to initiate spawning.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1064",
      "html": "<p>Rounded stones, sticks, and leaves over sand. The fish should be provided with half-pipe type refuges, which are also often used as spawning sites.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1064",
      "html": "<p>Adaptable omnivores, these fish will eat most foods from cucumber or zucchini slices to frozen bloodworm or dry flake foods.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1064",
      "html": "<p>Peaceful and not territorial, will not harm even the smallest fry.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1064",
      "html": "<p>Males grow short spines on the top of their heads and on the pectoral fins.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1064",
      "html": "<p>This is a very common species. Easily identified by the combination of barred fins and the dark lines on the ventral sides of the tail.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "references",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1064",
      "html": "<p>Bulletin de la Société Zoologique de France v. 33 (no. 6/7), pp 125.</p>"
    }
  ],
